          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Nathan prefers to call the most fundamental entities in their framework \"filaments,\" which give rise to elementary particles. They propose the term \"threads\" for simple composite particles, \"twines\" for atomic structures, \"yarns\" for molecular structures, \"bundles\" for interacting molecular systems, and \"ropes\" for gravitationally cohesive entities like planets and stars. They suggest the term \"heloids\" for stable orbital systems and \"loops\" or \"tethers\" for bodies not gravitationally bound to primary bodies at the astronomical scale. Nathan seeks to develop a comprehensive terminology for the various levels of entwined filament structures that intersect with the time surface in their framework."
          ]
